The docs suggest the Next method returns a bool, but that's not the case (Entry is an int).
	// Next advances the parser to the next sample. It returns false if no
	// more samples were read or an error occurred.
	Next() (Entry, error)

The docs were first added in d80a3de in 2017. Back then the signature was indeed func (p *Parser) Next() bool. But then it got refactored in 76a4a46 and the signature changed with it, yet docs stayed the same - and eventually made their way into the Parser interface.
However, the Protobuf parser does have the right wording: 5de2df7
